rediction data underpins the width-ratio analysis and the optimal control variate.\"\n491\t        },\n492\t        {\n493\t          \"category\": \"architectural_shift\",\n494\t          \"query\": \"double/debiased machine learning cross-fitting target parameter\",\n495\t          \"rationale\": \"Cross-fitted nuisance estimation with debiased inference motivates the recalibration step and its validity argument.\"\n496\t        },\n497\t        {\n498\t          \"category\": \"core_method\",\n499\t          \"query\": \"isotonic regression calibration of predictions\",\n500\t          \"rationale\": \"Isotonic and binned calibrators are the main recalibration maps g(Yhat) in the best-scoring method.\"\n501\t        },\n502\t        {\n503\t          \"category\": \"architectural_shift\",\n504\t          \"query\": \"stacking nonnegative least squares combining regression estimators\",\n505\t          \"rationale\": \"Cycle 3 uses NNLS-stacked calibrator libraries; need the stacking reference.\"\n506\t        },\n507\t        {\n508\t          \"category\": \"result_driven_theme\",\n509\t          \"query\": \"control variates variance reduction Monte Carlo regression adjustment survey sampling\",\n510\t          \"rationale\": \"PPI++ and recalibration are control-variate / model-assisted estimators; connects width gains to classical difference and regression estimators.\"\n511\t        },\n512\t        {\n513\t          \"category\": \"benchmark_context\",\n514\t          \"query\": \"Galaxy Zoo 2 morphological classifications; Retiring Adult folktables census datasets\",\n515\t          \"rationale\": \"Dataset provenance for the ppi-python example data used in evaluation; to be split by the retriever into separate dataset lookups.\"\n516\t        }\n517\t      ],\n518\t      \"result_driven_themes\": [\n519\t        \"Width gains over PPI++ are small on real datasets (log width ratio about 0.003-0.03) but larger on synthetic nonlinear miscalibration (about 0.