{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016QG9f2Yp9scNTNBA1HJ3X6","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Sealed final-plane evaluator (self-contained): confidence-interval width for a mean with fixed labels/unlabeled/predictor.\n\nProtocol (declared before evaluation). One episode = one independent labeled/unlabeled draw =\nreset + estimate (2 candidate RPCs). The evaluator draws n+N i.i.d. records with replacement from a\nfamily pool (or an analytic synthetic generator) with evaluator-private RNG keyed on a private master\nseed and (family, replicate), never on the candidate reset seed. Truth = pool mean of Y (analytic\nfor synthetic). Baselines (ppi_py 0.2.3): classical CLT, PPI (lam=1), PPI++ (power tuned).\n\nAggregation hierarchy (all weights fixed):\n  episode  -> covered_e in {0,1}, W_e (candidate width), P_e (PPI++), C_e (classical), L_e (PPI lam=1).\n              Invalid/missing/non-finite/timeout/baseline-failed episode: covered_e=0, W_e=10*C_e.\n  family   -> rho_f = sum W_e / sum P_e over that family's main episodes; s_f = -log(clip(rho_f,1e-3,1e3)).\n  plane    -> combined_score = mean over the 5 main families (weight 1/5 each) of s_f.\n  controls (const / perm / shift) are aggregated separately and enter only `correct` (gate).\n`correct` (validity only; claim assessment is the separate claim_status_code) = integrity AND exact one-sided binomial coverage tests (pooled level 0.01, per family\nBonferroni 0.01/5, failed episodes are misses) AND all controls pass their declared behaviour.\n\"\"\"\nimport time\n\n_T0 = time.monotonic()\n\nimport argparse\nimport base64\nimport collections\nimport hashlib\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nRESOURCE_SUBDIR = \"resources/final\"\nMASTER_SEED = 1923558401\nALPHA = 0.05\n# name -> (file, Y key, Yhat key, n, N)\nPOOLS = {\n    \"census_income\": (\"census_income.npz\", \"Y\", \"Yhat\", 500, 20000),\n    \"census_healthcare\": (\"census_healthcare.npz\", \"Y\", \"Yhat\", 500, 20000),\n    \"census_education\": (\"census_education.npz\", \"Y\", \"Yhat\", 500, 20000),\n    \"plankton\": (\"plankton.npz\", \"Y_unlabeled\", \"Yhat_unlabeled\", 500, 20000),\n}\nFILE_SHA256 = {\n    \"census_income.npz\": \"07db91fc27b7275763e9071768ed8125ec44640dcd49b9be6bae3e2335afcfb4\",\n    \"census_healthcare.npz\": \"86b01e52488e0415c04ad0c817ebceacb20903eb3dbf419548b89559d544e535\",\n    \"census_education.npz\": \"6a7c4c530b267d7ad3ebbdf99312ab7e1b57c9d41080b379cb7a7a22942ae4f0\",\n    \"plankton.npz\": \"b6e44b67805bd0f5df8e71a6ca5b1436e8bd6756a79de1c365de0e24788b00a1\",\n}\nMAIN_FAMILIES = [\"census_income\", \"census_healthcare\", \"census_education\", \"plankton\", \"synthetic\"]\nCONTROL_BASES = [\"census_income\", \"plankton\"]\nREPS_MAIN = 100\nREPS_CONTROL = 30\nSEEDS = [9101, 9102, 9103, 9104, 9105]\nSYNTH_REGIMES = [\n    (\"linear_calibrated\", -0.5, dict(a=-0.5, b=1.2, s=0.8, kind=\"linear\", noise_hat=0.5)),\n    (\"nonlinear_miscalibrated\", 3.0, dict(a=3.0, b=1.0, s=0.6, kind=\"cubic\", noise_hat=0.1)),\n    (\"uninformative\", 2.0, dict(a=2.0, b=1.0, s=1.2, kind=\"independent\", noise_hat=1.0)),\n    (\"heteroscedastic\", 0.0, dict(a=0.0, b=2.0, s=0.8, kind=\"hetero\", rate=0.5, noise_hat=0.4)),\n]\nSYNTH_N = [200, 500]\nSYNTH_BIG_N = [2000, 20000]\nWALL_SECONDS = 5400.0\nSMOKE_PLAN = [(\"census_income\", \"main\"), (\"census_healthcare\", \"main\"), (\"census_education\", \"main\"),\n              (\"plankton\", \"main\"), (\"synthetic\", \"main\"),\n              (\"census_income\", \"const\"), (\"census_income\", \"perm\"), (\"census_income\", \"shift\")]\n# ==== PLANE CONFIG (end) ====\n\nPROXY_PATH = \"/broker-code/candidate_proxy.py\"\nCONTROL_TYPES = [\"const\", \"perm\", \"shift\"]\nRESET_TIMEOUT = 4.0\nRPC_CAP = 3.0\nSTARTUP_ALLOWANCE = 60.0\nFINISH_RESERVE = 15.0\nBROKER_OVERHEAD = 1.0\nNATIVE_OVERHEAD = 3.0\nSMOKE_WALL = 110.0\nSMOKE_STARTUP = 5.0\nSMOKE_FINISH = 5.0\nWIRE_LIMIT = 